er hero persona is  stature eventually she's a part of The  Young Avengers who also has a teammate  named iron lad interesting an Iron Man  like young hero who is eventually  revealed to be king from the future see  all these complicated stories already  spiraling out of this number 2 if you  wanted to go smaller potatoes for our  next big-time villain and  not go all universe ending event II  maybe you could turn to one of Spidey's  villains especially the one that has  such a big impact on the Marvel Comics  universe that's right I'm talking about  Norman Osborn now I know we've seen two  versions of Norman so far but for good  reason he's one of the most important  characters to Peter Parker and I know  Marvel Studios and if they had their  writers worked on infinity war in Civil  War on Captain America Winter Soldier  they could really turn him into a real  powerhouse now imagine this after  infinity War part 2 we realized that the  sokovia cords aren't really working we  need a better solution in the UN  handpicks new individuals to make a  better Avengers team who could protect  them against cosmic and  extra-dimensional  threats and who better to lead them than  a powerful influential businessman who's  willing to put his life on the line much  like Tony Stark  that's where Norman comes in and this  could be very similar to his run as the  leader of the Dark Avengers actually  this is where the iron Patriot suit was  introduced fun fact this would also lead  to a team of villains to face off  against our heroes much like the Masters  of evil or you could possibly go with  something closer to the sinister six  those are just some extra ideas but  since we had the tease of someone buying  Avengers tower in spider-man homecoming  and Sonny Bert's working for someone  else in a man and the wasp it would be  interesting to learn that Norman has  been working in secret for quite some  time in the MCU number three let's go  back to our huge cosmic level threats  for